## Cleaning the AI Workspace

One of the practical goals of NovaSpire Unity 1.3 is **workspace
cleanup**.

AI workspaces often collect digital garbage over time. This includes
old prompts, abandoned documents, duplicate agents, outdated modules,
unused files, failed experiments, and unclear system instructions.

NovaSpire Unity 1.3 introduces a more disciplined structure.

Instead of allowing everything to remain scattered, the workspace can
be organized into clear categories:

- active agents
- inactive agents
- archived agents
- connector portals
- system documentation
- task modules
- personality modules
- tool modules
- testing modules
- production modules
- deprecated files
- core AI instructions

This makes the workspace easier to understand and easier to maintain.

A clean workspace also makes the AI more reliable. When the AI knows
which systems are current, which agents are active, and which
instructions are valid, it can operate with less confusion and better
consistency.

